           'admission to the 6-Year Integrated B.Tech Program at RGUKT Basar '
           'are as follows:\n'
           '\n'
           'Admission to the 1st year of the 6-Year Integrated B.Tech Program '
           'will be based on merit in the Grade Point Average (GPA) and Grade '
           'obtained in each subject of SSC (10th class) or any other '
           'equivalent examination recognized by the state.\n'
           '\n'
           'Additionally, for the purpose of admission, the following criteria '
           'will be considered:\n'
           '\n'
           '1. Admissions will be based on merit in the Grade Point Average '
           '(GPA) and Grade obtained in each subject of SSC (10th class) or '
           'any other equivalent examination recognized by the state.\n'
           '2. A deprivation score of 0.4 prescribed by the state Government '
           'under Statute 13 (3) shall be added to the 10th class GPA of those '
           'applicants who studied in non-residential Government Schools '
           'including the Zillaparishad and Municipal Schools, with an '
           'objective of providing weightage to the socio-economically '
           'challenged students in the admission process.\n'
           '3. At RGUKT-Basar, admissions to 85% of the total available seats '
           'shall be reserved for the Local Candidates (Telangana State) and '
           'the remaining 15% of the seats shall be un-reserved (these seats '
           'will be filled with students from both States of Telangana and '
           'Andhra Pradesh based on merit) as specified in the Presidential '
           'Order 371 Article D in consonance to Section 95 of the A.P. '
           'Reorganization Act, 2014.\n'
           '\n'
           'Please note that the eligibility criteria may be subject to '
           'change, and it is always best to check with the college or '
           'university for the most up-to-date information.',
