 'context': [Document(id='5eca804e-7ff7-4a14-8fa2-cb330afdfc21', metadata={'creationdate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'creator': 'Edited with https://pdfresizer.com', 'moddate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'page': 4, 'page_label': '5', 'producer': 'GPL Ghostscript 9.26', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/acadamic/Academic_Regulations_Hand_Book.pdf', 'total_pages': 1021}, page_content='of Rs. 36,000/- for PUC and Rs.40,000/- for B.Tech progra mmes and any other miscellaneous \nfees(examination fees etc., if applicable). \n \n \nVI. SCHEME OF INSTRUCTION AND EXAMINATION \n1. Instruction to the various courses in each semester of th e six-year integrated program, shall be provided by \nthe University as per the schemes of instructions and syllabi prescribed in the syllabus book. \n2. The distribution of marks / grade* for courses based on Co ntinuous Internal Evaluation (CIE) and the End \nSemester Examination (ESE) shall be as follows. \nSubject Continuous \nInternal Evaluation \n(CIE) \nEnd Semester \nExamination (ESE) \nEach theory subject 40 60 \nEach Laboratory 40 60 \nEach drawing subject/Lab 50 50 \nSeminar -- 100 \nComprehensive Viva -- 100 \nInternship -- 100 \nProject -- 100 \n \n *Grades are allotted based on the marks secured in Conti nuous Internal Evaluation and End Semester \nExamination as per the following criteria. \nï The evaluation of each theory subject for maximum of 100  marks will be done as per guidelines given \nbelow: \ni.  Out of 40 internal marks of theory subject, 10 marks are f or the Assignments/Tutorials/Quizzes \netc., in the course, the rest of the 30 marks are based on  Monthly Tests; weightage for each \nmonthly test is 15 marks, out of which Five marks for Part-A  consisting of objective and short \nanswer questions and 10 marks for Part-B consisting of subjective questions.  \nii. Three Monthly tests will be conducted in each semester.   Best 2 out of 3 Monthly Tests is \nconsidered in evaluation for 30 marks and 10 marks is awarded based on the assignments given \nin the particular course from time to time (At least three assignments to be given in engineering \nsubjects and at least six assignments to be given in PUC subjects). \niii. Out of 60 marks end semester examination of theory  subject, question paper consists of subjective \nquestions covering all the units of the syllabus.'),
             Document(id='74913dd9-eff5-474d-89dc-405ec1c19dc2', metadata={'creationdate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'creator': 'Edited with https://pdfresizer.com', 'moddate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'page': 4, 'page_label': '5', 'producer': 'GPL Ghostscript 9.26', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/acadamic/Academic_Regulations_Hand_Book.pdf', 'total_pages': 1021}, page_content='of Rs. 36,000/- for PUC and Rs.40,000/- for B.Tech progra mmes and any other miscellaneous \nfees(examination fees etc., if applicable). \n \n \nVI. SCHEME OF INSTRUCTION AND EXAMINATION \n1. Instruction to the various courses in each semester of th e six-year integrated program, shall be provided by \nthe University as per the schemes of instructions and syllabi prescribed in the syllabus book. \n2. The distribution of marks / grade* for courses based on Co ntinuous Internal Evaluation (CIE) and the End \nSemester Examination (ESE) shall be as follows. \nSubject Continuous \nInternal Evaluation \n(CIE) \nEnd Semester \nExamination (ESE) \nEach theory subject 40 60 \nEach Laboratory 40 60 \nEach drawing subject/Lab 50 50 \nSeminar -- 100 \nComprehensive Viva -- 100 \nInternship -- 100 \nProject -- 100 \n \n *Grades are allotted based on the marks secured in Conti nuous Internal Evaluation and End Semester \nExamination as per the following criteria. \nï The evaluation of each theory subject for maximum of 100  marks will be done as per guidelines given \nbelow: \ni.  Out of 40 internal marks of theory subject, 10 marks are f or the Assignments/Tutorials/Quizzes \netc., in the course, the rest of the 30 marks are based on  Monthly Tests; weightage for each \nmonthly test is 15 marks, out of which Five marks for Part-A  consisting of objective and short \nanswer questions and 10 marks for Part-B consisting of subjective questions.  \nii. Three Monthly tests will be conducted in each semester.   Best 2 out of 3 Monthly Tests is \nconsidered in evaluation for 30 marks and 10 marks is awarded based on the assignments given \nin the particular course from time to time (At least three assignments to be given in engineering \nsubjects and at least six assignments to be given in PUC subjects). \niii. Out of 60 marks end semester examination of theory  subject, question paper consists of subjective \nquestions covering all the units of the syllabus.'),
             Document(id='984f8d38-e07d-4458-8c87-c84d861765a8', metadata={'creationdate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'creator': 'Edited with https://pdfresizer.com', 'moddate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'page': 6, 'page_label': '7', 'producer': 'GPL Ghostscript 9.26', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/acadamic/Academic_Regulations_Hand_Book.pdf', 'total_pages': 1021}, page_content='VII. GRADING SYSTEM AND AWARD OF DIVISION \n1. For the PUC program of the 6-year integrated course, an absolute grading system is used to award \ngrades to students. The grading table is given below for PUC program: \nS. \nNo \nPerformance Marks Range Letter Grade Grade point \nvalue per \ncredit \n1 Excellent 90 ñ 100 Ex 10 \n2 Very good 80 ñ 89 A 9 \n3 Good 70 ñ 79 B 8 \n4 Fair 60 ñ 69 C 7 \n5 Average 50 ñ 59 D 6 \n6 Pass 40-49 P 5 \n7 Remedial / Fail < 40 R 0 \n \ni. Highest possible CGPA in the system is 10.00 \nii. Pass Requirements: \nï Below mentioned minimum marks for Pass are applicable for th e students admitted into PUC from \nthe academic year 2016-17. \na. Theory ñ A minimum of 40% marks in end semester examination and an overall of minimum \n40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \nb. Laboratory - A minimum of 50% marks in end semester examinat ion and an overall of \nminimum 50% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade) \n If a candidate in any semester examination of the progra m fails to secure the minimum marks/grade in any \nsubject, then he/she shall have to appear for supplementary/remedial examination only in the failed subject \nof the semester. \nï Below mentioned minimum marks for Pass are applicable for th e students admitted into PUC \nbefore the academic year 2016-17. \na. Theory ñ Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \nb. Laboratory - Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \n If a candidate in any semester examination of the prog ram fails to secure the minimum marks/grade in \nany subject, then he/she shall have to appear for supp lementary/remedial examination only in the \nfailed subject of the semester. \niii. For results evaluated using the Absolute Grading m ethod for PUC batches, results are to be \nmoderated by a Committee convened by the Controller of Examinations. The Committee comprises of \nthe following: \na) Vice Chancellor / Director - Chairman \nb) Dean (Academics) - Member'),
             Document(id='01834812-f30f-4c51-848e-6c479a6f0a12', metadata={'creationdate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'creator': 'Edited with https://pdfresizer.com', 'moddate': '2020-01-25T10:01:47+01:00', 'page': 6, 'page_label': '7', 'producer': 'GPL Ghostscript 9.26', 'source': '../rguktBasarDataset/acadamic/Academic_Regulations_Hand_Book.pdf', 'total_pages': 1021}, page_content='VII. GRADING SYSTEM AND AWARD OF DIVISION \n1. For the PUC program of the 6-year integrated course, an absolute grading system is used to award \ngrades to students. The grading table is given below for PUC program: \nS. \nNo \nPerformance Marks Range Letter Grade Grade point \nvalue per \ncredit \n1 Excellent 90 ñ 100 Ex 10 \n2 Very good 80 ñ 89 A 9 \n3 Good 70 ñ 79 B 8 \n4 Fair 60 ñ 69 C 7 \n5 Average 50 ñ 59 D 6 \n6 Pass 40-49 P 5 \n7 Remedial / Fail < 40 R 0 \n \ni. Highest possible CGPA in the system is 10.00 \nii. Pass Requirements: \nï Below mentioned minimum marks for Pass are applicable for th e students admitted into PUC from \nthe academic year 2016-17. \na. Theory ñ A minimum of 40% marks in end semester examination and an overall of minimum \n40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \nb. Laboratory - A minimum of 50% marks in end semester examinat ion and an overall of \nminimum 50% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade) \n If a candidate in any semester examination of the progra m fails to secure the minimum marks/grade in any \nsubject, then he/she shall have to appear for supplementary/remedial examination only in the failed subject \nof the semester. \nï Below mentioned minimum marks for Pass are applicable for th e students admitted into PUC \nbefore the academic year 2016-17. \na. Theory ñ Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \nb. Laboratory - Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade) \n If a candidate in any semester examination of the prog ram fails to secure the minimum marks/grade in \nany subject, then he/she shall have to appear for supp lementary/remedial examination only in the \nfailed subject of the semester. \niii. For results evaluated using the Absolute Grading m ethod for PUC batches, results are to be \nmoderated by a Committee convened by the Controller of Examinations. The Committee comprises of \nthe following: \na) Vice Chancellor / Director - Chairman \nb) Dean (Academics) - Member')],
 'input': 'Provide me the Grading criteria in exams'}
2025-04-12 15:19:39,188 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:59 - Response from the agent: {'response': {'answer': "According to the RGUKT Basar's guidelines, the "
                        'grading criteria for exams are as follows:\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**PUC Program (6-year Integrated Course)**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '* For students admitted from the academic year '
                        '2016-17:\n'
                        '\t+ Theory subjects: 40% marks in end semester '
                        'examination and an overall of minimum 40% marks in '
                        'the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                        '\t+ Laboratory subjects: 50% marks in end semester '
                        'examination and an overall of minimum 50% marks in '
                        'the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade)\n'
                        '* For students admitted before the academic year '
                        '2016-17:\n'
                        '\t+ Theory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE '
                        'plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                        '\t+ Laboratory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE '
                        'plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**Grading Table for PUC Program:**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '| S. No | Performance | Marks Range | Letter Grade | '
                        'Grade Point |\n'
                        '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
                        '| 1 | Excellent | 90-100 | Ex | 10 |\n'
                        '| 2 | Very Good | 80-89 | A | 9 |\n'
                        '| 3 | Good | 70-79 | B | 8 |\n'
                        '| 4 | Fair | 60-69 | C | 7 |\n'
                        '| 5 | Average | 50-59 | D | 6 |\n'
                        '| 6 | Pass | 40-49 | P | 5 |\n'
                        '| 7 | Remedial/Fail | < 40 | R | 0 |\n'
                        '\n'
                        'The highest possible CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point '
                        'Average) in the system is 10.00.\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**End Semester Examination (ESE) and Continuous '
                        'Internal Evaluation (CIE)**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '* Each theory subject: 40 internal marks (out of '
                        'which 10 marks are for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, '
                        'etc.) and 60 marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                        '* Each laboratory subject: 50 internal marks and 50 '
                        'marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                        '* Each drawing subject/lab: 50 internal marks and 50 '
                        'marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                        '* Seminar, Comprehensive Viva, Internship, and '
                        'Project: 100 marks each.\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**Evaluation Criteria for Theory Subjects:**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '* 10 marks for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, etc.\n'
                        '* 30 marks for monthly tests (best 2 out of 3 monthly '
                        'tests considered)\n'
                        '* 10 marks for assignments given in the particular '
                        'course from time to time\n'
                        '* 60 marks for the end semester examination\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**Evaluation Criteria for Laboratory Subjects:**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '* 50 internal marks\n'
                        '* 50 marks for the end semester examination\n'
                        '\n'
                        '**Grading System for PUC Program:**\n'
                        '\n'
                        '* The grading system is based on the Absolute Grading '
                        'method.\n'
                        '* The grading committee, comprising the '
                        'Vice-Chancellor/Director, Dean (Academics), and other '
                        'members, moderates the results for PUC batches.\n'
                        '\n'
                        'Please note that these grading criteria are specific '
                        'to the PUC program and may vary for other programs or '
                        'courses offered by RGUKT Basar.',
