2025-04-12 15:19:39,203 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:60 - Response answer from the agent: According to the RGUKT Basar's guidelines, the grading criteria for exams are as follows:

**PUC Program (6-year Integrated Course)**

* For students admitted from the academic year 2016-17:
	+ Theory subjects: 40% marks in end semester examination and an overall of minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)
	+ Laboratory subjects: 50% marks in end semester examination and an overall of minimum 50% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade)
* For students admitted before the academic year 2016-17:
	+ Theory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)
	+ Laboratory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)

**Grading Table for PUC Program:**

| S. No | Performance | Marks Range | Letter Grade | Grade Point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Excellent | 90-100 | Ex | 10 |
| 2 | Very Good | 80-89 | A | 9 |
| 3 | Good | 70-79 | B | 8 |
| 4 | Fair | 60-69 | C | 7 |
| 5 | Average | 50-59 | D | 6 |
| 6 | Pass | 40-49 | P | 5 |
| 7 | Remedial/Fail | < 40 | R | 0 |

The highest possible CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point Average) in the system is 10.00.

**End Semester Examination (ESE) and Continuous Internal Evaluation (CIE)**

* Each theory subject: 40 internal marks (out of which 10 marks are for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, etc.) and 60 marks for the end semester examination.
* Each laboratory subject: 50 internal marks and 50 marks for the end semester examination.
* Each drawing subject/lab: 50 internal marks and 50 marks for the end semester examination.
* Seminar, Comprehensive Viva, Internship, and Project: 100 marks each.

**Evaluation Criteria for Theory Subjects:**

* 10 marks for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, etc.
* 30 marks for monthly tests (best 2 out of 3 monthly tests considered)
* 10 marks for assignments given in the particular course from time to time
* 60 marks for the end semester examination

**Evaluation Criteria for Laboratory Subjects:**

* 50 internal marks
* 50 marks for the end semester examination

**Grading System for PUC Program:**

* The grading system is based on the Absolute Grading method.
* The grading committee, comprising the Vice-Chancellor/Director, Dean (Academics), and other members, moderates the results for PUC batches.

Please note that these grading criteria are specific to the PUC program and may vary for other programs or courses offered by RGUKT Basar.
