                  {'content': "According to the RGUKT Basar's guidelines, the "
                              'grading criteria for exams are as follows:\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**PUC Program (6-year Integrated Course)**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '* For students admitted from the academic year '
                              '2016-17:\n'
                              '\t+ Theory subjects: 40% marks in end semester '
                              'examination and an overall of minimum 40% marks '
                              'in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                              '\t+ Laboratory subjects: 50% marks in end '
                              'semester examination and an overall of minimum '
                              '50% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade)\n'
                              '* For students admitted before the academic '
                              'year 2016-17:\n'
                              '\t+ Theory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in the '
                              'ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                              '\t+ Laboratory subjects: Minimum 40% marks in '
                              'the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**Grading Table for PUC Program:**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '| S. No | Performance | Marks Range | Letter '
                              'Grade | Grade Point |\n'
                              '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
                              '| 1 | Excellent | 90-100 | Ex | 10 |\n'
                              '| 2 | Very Good | 80-89 | A | 9 |\n'
                              '| 3 | Good | 70-79 | B | 8 |\n'
                              '| 4 | Fair | 60-69 | C | 7 |\n'
                              '| 5 | Average | 50-59 | D | 6 |\n'
                              '| 6 | Pass | 40-49 | P | 5 |\n'
                              '| 7 | Remedial/Fail | < 40 | R | 0 |\n'
                              '\n'
                              'The highest possible CGPA (Cumulative Grade '
                              'Point Average) in the system is 10.00.\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**End Semester Examination (ESE) and Continuous '
                              'Internal Evaluation (CIE)**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '* Each theory subject: 40 internal marks (out '
                              'of which 10 marks are for '
                              'assignments/tutorials/quizzes, etc.) and 60 '
                              'marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                              '* Each laboratory subject: 50 internal marks '
                              'and 50 marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                              '* Each drawing subject/lab: 50 internal marks '
                              'and 50 marks for the end semester examination.\n'
                              '* Seminar, Comprehensive Viva, Internship, and '
                              'Project: 100 marks each.\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**Evaluation Criteria for Theory Subjects:**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '* 10 marks for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, '
                              'etc.\n'
                              '* 30 marks for monthly tests (best 2 out of 3 '
                              'monthly tests considered)\n'
                              '* 10 marks for assignments given in the '
                              'particular course from time to time\n'
                              '* 60 marks for the end semester examination\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**Evaluation Criteria for Laboratory '
                              'Subjects:**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '* 50 internal marks\n'
                              '* 50 marks for the end semester examination\n'
                              '\n'
                              '**Grading System for PUC Program:**\n'
                              '\n'
                              '* The grading system is based on the Absolute '
                              'Grading method.\n'
                              '* The grading committee, comprising the '
                              'Vice-Chancellor/Director, Dean (Academics), and '
                              'other members, moderates the results for PUC '
                              'batches.\n'
                              '\n'
                              'Please note that these grading criteria are '
                              'specific to the PUC program and may vary for '
                              'other programs or courses offered by RGUKT '
                              'Basar.',
