2025-04-12 15:23:09,368 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:60 - Response answer from the agent: According to the RGUKT Basar's guidelines, the grading criteria for exams are as follows:

**Theory Subjects:**

* Evaluation of each theory subject for a maximum of 100 marks will be done as per the following guidelines:
	+ Out of 40 internal marks, 10 marks are for assignments/tutorials/quizzes, etc.
	+ The rest of the 30 marks are based on monthly tests, with a weightage of 15 marks for each monthly test.
	+ Out of the 15 marks for each monthly test, 5 marks are for Part-A (objective and short-answer questions) and 10 marks are for Part-B (subjective questions).
	+ Three monthly tests will be conducted in each semester.
	+ Best 2 out of 3 monthly tests will be considered in evaluation for 30 marks.
	+ 10 marks will be awarded based on assignments given in the particular course from time to time (at least three assignments to be given in engineering subjects and at least six assignments to be given in PUC subjects).
* Out of 60 marks for the end semester examination, the question paper will consist of subjective questions covering all the units of the syllabus.

**Laboratory Subjects:**

* Evaluation of each laboratory subject will be based on:
	+ 50 internal marks
	+ 50 marks for the end semester examination

**Drawing Subjects/Lab:**

* Evaluation of each drawing subject/lab will be based on:
	+ 50 internal marks
	+ 50 marks for the end semester examination

**Seminar, Comprehensive Viva, Internship, and Project:**

* Evaluation of these subjects will be based on:
	+ 100 marks each

**Grading Criteria:**

* The grading system is based on the Absolute Grading method.
* The grading committee, comprising the Vice-Chancellor/Director, Dean (Academics), and other members, moderates the results.

**Grading Table:**

| S. No | Performance | Marks Range | Letter Grade | Grade Point |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Excellent | 90-100 | Ex | 10 |
| 2 | Very Good | 80-89 | A | 9 |
| 3 | Good | 70-79 | B | 8 |
| 4 | Fair | 60-69 | C | 7 |
| 5 | Average | 50-59 | D | 6 |
| 6 | Pass | 40-49 | P | 5 |
| 7 | Remedial/Fail | < 40 | R | 0 |

The highest possible CGPA (Cumulative Grade Point Average) in the system is 10.00.

Please note that these grading criteria are specific to the PUC program and may vary for other programs or courses offered by RGUKT Basar.
