	+ Laboratory: Minimum 50% marks in end semester examination and an overall of minimum 50% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., D grade)
* For students admitted into PUC before the academic year 2016-17:
	+ Theory: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)
	+ Laboratory: Minimum 40% marks in the ESE plus CIE (i.e., P grade)

Note: If a candidate fails to secure the minimum marks/grade in any subject, they shall have to appear for supplementary/remedial examination only in the failed subject of the semester.
