2025-04-12 17:12:10,422 - INFO - chat_app.services.impl.chat_service_impl - chat_service_impl.generate_response:60 - Response answer from the agent: Here's a sample email that you can use as a template:

Subject: Feedback on Mess Food Quality

Dear Honorable Vice Chancellor,

I hope this email finds you well. I am writing to bring to your attention the dissatisfaction that many of us students are experiencing with the quality of food served in the mess. As you may be aware, the mess is a crucial aspect of campus life, and it plays a significant role in our overall well-being.

Unfortunately, the recent quality of food has been subpar, and many of us are not feeling satisfied with the options available. The food is often bland, overcooked, or spoiled, which is affecting our health and appetite. We understand that the mess is managed by a third-party contractor, but as students, we believe that it is our right to have access to nutritious and hygienic food.

We would like to request that you take immediate action to address this issue. We propose the following:

* Conduct a thorough audit of the mess operations, including food procurement, storage, and preparation.
* Improve the quality of food by sourcing fresh ingredients and implementing proper food handling and storage procedures.
* Increase the variety of options available to cater to different dietary preferences and restrictions.
* Consider hiring additional staff to ensure that the mess is adequately staffed during peak hours.

We believe that these steps will significantly improve the quality of food and overall dining experience for students. We would appreciate it if you could provide us with an update on the actions being taken to address this issue.

Thank you for your time and attention to this matter. We look forward to hearing from you soon.

Sincerely,

[Your Name]

cc: [Name of Student Council/Representative, if any]

Please note that you should customize the email to fit your specific situation and concerns. Also, be sure to proofread your email for grammar, spelling, and tone before sending it to the Vice Chancellor.
