2025-04-12 18:32:00,104 - INFO - chat_app.agent.agent_executor - agent_executor.execute:152 - Generated Response: {'answer': 'RGUKT Basar follows a combination of absolute and relative grading '
           'for evaluation and award of grades. The grade cut-off for the '
           'absolute grading is as follows:\n'
           '\n'
           'S. No Marks Range Grade Grade points per credit\n'
           '1 90 ñ 100 Ex 10\n'
           '2 80 ñ 89 A 9\n'
           '3 70 ñ 79 B 8\n'
           '4 60 ñ 69 C 7\n'
           '5 50 ñ 59 D 6\n'
           '6 < 50 R 0\n'
           '\n'
           'The process for awarding grades in engineering streams is as '
           'follows:\n'
           '\n'
           'i. In each subject, marks awarded are compiled into a cumulative '
           'frequency table.\n'
           'ii. A new cut-off mark for each grade is obtained following the '
           'relative grading system based on the percentage number of students '
           'expected to fall in each grade.\n'
           'iii. New cut-off marks for awarding grades are obtained by '
           'comparing the relative grading cut-off marks to the absolute '
           'grading cut-off marks. The lower of the two is taken as the new '
           'cut-off mark, subject to a maximum deviation of 10 marks from the '
           'fixed grading system.\n'
           'iv. In each case, the new cut-off is limited to ±10 marks from the '
           'cut-offs of the fixed grading system.\n'
           'v. In case the fixed grading cut-off > relative grading cut-off > '
           '10, then the new cut-off is obtained as fixed grading cut-off ñ '
           '10.\n'
           '\n'
           'The highest possible CGPA in the system is 10.00. The pass '
           'requirements are:\n'
           '\n'
           'a. Theory: minimum marks for Pass is 50% or cut-off for D-grade, '
           'whichever is lower.\n'
           'b. Laboratory/Internship/Project/Comprehensive Viva/Seminar: '
           'minimum marks for Pass is 50% or cut-off for D-grade, whichever is '
           'lower.',
 'chat_history': [],
